    eslavos: { nombre: "Slavic tribes", pais: "Eastern Europe", lider: "Vesna", estilo: "Forest and endurance", descripcion: "It fights where the enemy doesn't want to go. In forests and hills it's almost impossible to dislodge, and its sorceress heals whoever fights beside her. In open ground and without heavy cavalry, it suffers.",
      resumen: "Fights where the enemy doesn't want to go. Your heroine is Vesna, a sorceress who casts a bolt two hexes away and heals 10 to the troops fighting beside her at the end of your turn. Its trait, Children of the Forest, gives +3 defence in forest and hill and lets your foot troops cross woods as if they were plains, and her power, Winter, takes 1 movement off the whole enemy army. Its own unit is the forest guardian, a better spearman who is almost immovable in the woods. In exchange, it has no heavy cavalry and it suffers in the open.",
      rasgo: { nombre: "Children of the forest", texto: "Your troops in forests or hills get +3 defence, and those on foot cross forests as if they were plains." }, poder: { nombre: "Winter", texto: "Until your next turn, every enemy troop moves 1 less (never below 1)." } },
